https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/github.com","site_name":"GitHub"},{"url":"https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/pull/71499#1","title":"fix(install): select supported Python on Termux by yinkev · Pull Request #71499 · NousResearch/hermes-agent - Skip to content","snippet":"probe every explicitly supported Termux interpreter in order:python3.11, python3.12, then python3.13, before falling back to default python ... a host with default python 3.14 ... python3.12 or python3.13 still skipped the supported interpreter and entered a doomed install/failure path. ... - defaultpython 3.14 + only python3.13 available → selects 3.13...","published_at":"2026-07-24T16:00:00Z","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/github.com","site_name":"GitHub"},{"url":"https://linuxhandbook.com/using-theharvester/","title":"PenTesting 101: Using TheHarvester for OSINT and Reconnaissance","snippet":"Installing TheHarvester If you're not using Kali Linux, you can easily install TheHarvester from its GitHub repository. ### Option A: Using apt (Kali Linux / Debian/Ubuntu) sudo apt update && sudo apt install theharvester ### Option B: Installing from source (Latest Version) git clone https://github.com/laramies/theHarvester.git","published_at":"2025-10-21T16:00:00Z","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/linuxhandbook.com","site_name":"Linux Handbook"},{"url":"https://github.com/pathintegral-institute/mcpm.sh/pull/333#1","title":"Relax pydantic upper bound to support Python 3.14 by sporkd · Pull Request #333 · pathintegral-institute/mcpm.sh","snippet":"pydantic >=2.13 depends on pydantic-core >=2.46 which ships cp314 wheels. ... Run `uv lock --upgrade-package pydantic --upgrade-package pydantic-core` to resolve pydantic 2.13.4 and pydantic-core 2.46.4, which ship pre-built wheels for Python 3.14.","published_at":"2026-05-06T16:00:00Z","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/github.com","site_name":"GitHub"},{"url":"https://github.com/termux-user-repository/tur/issues/508","title":"[Package]: Pydantic · Issue #508 · termux-user-repository/tur","snippet":"Addedpydantic-core via termux-user-repository/pypi-wheel-builder@c6af49d. Now this package is able to be installed though pip. python -m pip install pydantic --extra-index-url https://termux-user-repository.github.io/pypi/","published_at":"2023-07-23T16:00:00Z","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/github.com","site_name":"GitHub"},{"url":"https://github.com/Eutalix/termux-spotdl-installer#1","title":"GitHub - Eutalix/termux-spotdl-installer: 🚀 Fast & Optimized spotDL installer for Android (Termux). Skip Rust compilation with pre-built wheels, auto-configure storage, and setup shortcuts · GitHub - GitHub - Eutalix/termux-spotdl-installer: 🚀 Fast & Optimized spotDL installer for Android (Termux). Skip Rust compilation with p...","snippet":"It uses pre-compiled `pydantic-core` wheels from android-pydantic-core to install SpotDL in **seconds** instead of minutes. ... Open Termux and run this single command ... 3. Installs SpotDL using optimized Android wheels.","published_at":"2026-01-30T16:00:00Z","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/github.com","site_name":"GitHub"},{"url":"https://cosyra.com/guides/rust-on-termux.html","title":"Rust on Termux: What Works and What Kills Your Build","snippet":"Because rustup does not supportaarch64-linux-android as a host platform. The installer resolves your host triple, looks for matching binaries in the stable channel, finds none, and stops with \"target 'aarch64-linux-android'","published_at":"2025-08-31T16:00:00Z","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/cosyra.com","site_name":"Cosyra"},{"url":"https://pydantic.com.cn/","title":"欢迎使用 Pydantic¶","snippet":"我们意识到具有讽刺意味的是，Pydantic V1 在其验证中并不严格，所以如果我们很“吹毛求疵”的话，在 V2 版本之前，“Pydantic”是一个用词不当的名称😉 ... 速度——Pydantic 的核心验证逻辑是用 Rust 编写的。因此...","published_at":null,"site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/pydantic.com.cn","site_name":"pydantic.com.cn"}],"status":"FINISHED"},{"type":"RESPONSE","content":"**النتيجة: الفشل ليس خطأ منك. السبب هو أن `theHarvester 5.0.0` يجبر على تثبيت `pydantic-core` بإصدار قديم، وهذا الإصدار لا يملك نسخة جاهزة (wheel) لـ Python 3.14 على Termux، فيحاول البناء من Rust ويفشل.**\n\n---\n\n### لماذا فشل التحديد بالضبط\n\nانظر إلى السطر في السجل:\n\n```\nCollecting pydantic-core==2.46.5\n```\n\n`theHarvester 5.0.0` يطلب `pydantic>=2.9.0`، وهذا يقود pip إلى تحميل **pydantic 2.13.5**، الذي يعتمد بدوره على **pydantic-core 2.46.5**. هذا الإصدار تحديداً من pydantic-core لا يملك wheel لـ Python 3.14 على Termux، فينتقل pip إلى البناء من المصدر عبر Rust، ويفشل لأن `rustup` لا يدعم `aarch64-unknown-linux-android` .\n\nالمشكلة ليست في theHarvester نفسه، بل في سلسلة الاعتماديات التي تسحب pydantic-core قديم.\n\n### الحل: تثبيت pydantic-core من مصدر Android مخصص\n\nيوجد مشروع يُدعى `android-pydantic-core` يوفر نسخاً مجمّعة مسبقاً لـ Termux . جرّب:\n\n```bash\npip install pydantic-core --extra-index-url https://eutalix.github.io/android-pydantic-core/\n```\n\nثم أعد تثبيت theHarvester:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/theHarvester\npip install .\n```\n\n**لكن** — المشروع المذكور يغطي حتى Python 3.13 فقط . وأنت على Python 3.14. لذا قد يفشل هذا أيضاً.\n\n### البديل الأكثر واقعية: خفّض Python إلى 3.13\n\nTermux الآن يوزع Python 3.14 افتراضياً، لكن يمكنك الحصول على Python 3.13 من حزمة `aws-cli`:\n\n```bash\npkg install aws-cli\nln -sf $PREFIX/lib/aws-cli/python3.13 $PREFIX/bin/python3.13\n```\n\nثم أنشئ بيئة افتراضية بـ Python 3.13، وثبّت theHarvester فيها .\n\n### الخيار الثالث: استخدم pydantic v1\n\nالمشروع `harvester-windows` على PyPI يستخدم `uv` بدلاً من pip . لكن `uv` نفسه يعاني من نفس مشاكل البناء على Termux.\n\nالنسخ القديمة جداً من theHarvester (ما قبل 4.x) كانت تعتمد على pydantic v1، وهو **Python خالص بلا Rust** . لكن هذه النسخ قد لا تعمل مع Python 3.14 أيضاً.\n\n### الأسهل الآن: استخدم أدوات بديلة\n\nبدلاً من الاستمرار في مقارعة theHarvester، ثبّت أدوات OSINT التي تعمل مباشرة على Termux بلا مشاكل بناء:\n\n```bash\npip install holehe sherlock-project\n```\n\nهذه Python خالص، بلا Rust، بلا pydantic-core. تعمل فوراً.\n\n**هل تريد أن نستمر في محاولة إصلاح theHarvester، أم ننتقل إلى الأدوات البديلة مباشرة؟**"}]},{"id":99,"parent_id":98,"role":"USER","status":"FINISHED","thinking_enabled":false,"search_enabled":true,"accumulated_token_usage":85200,"inserted_at":"2026-10-03T15:16:18.058Z","fragments":[{"type":"REQUEST","content":"~/theHarvester $ pip install pydantic-core --extra-index-url https://eutalix.github.io/android-pydantic-core/\nLooking in indexes: https://pypi.org/simple, https://eutalix.github.io/android-pydantic-core/\nCollecting pydantic-core\n  Downloading pydantic_core-2.49.0-cp314-cp314-android_24_arm64_v8a.whl (2.0 MB)\n     ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 2.0/2.0 MB 1.0 MB/s  0:00:01\nCollecting typing-extensions>=4.16.0 (from pydantic-core)\n  Using cached typing_extensions-4.16.0-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (3.3 kB)\nUsing cached typing_extensions-4.16.0-py3-none-any.whl (45 kB)\nInstalling collected packages: typing-extensions, pydantic-core\nSuccessfully installed pydantic-core-2.49.0 typing-extensions-4.16.0\n~/theHarvester $ cd ~/theHarvester\npip install .\nProcessing ./.\n  Installing build dependencies ... done\n  Getting requirements to build wheel ... done\n  Preparing metadata (pyproject.toml) ... done\nCollecting aiodns==4.0.4 (from theHarvester==5.0.0)\n  Using cached aiodns-4.0.4-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (9.0 kB)\nCollecting aiohttp==3.14.3 (from theHarvester==5.0.0)\n  Using cached aiohttp-3.14.3-cp314-cp314-android_24_arm64_v8a.whl.metadata (8.3 kB)\nCollecting aiohttp-socks==0.11.0 (from theHarvester==5.0.0)\n  Using cached aiohttp_socks-0.11.0-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (3.6 kB)\nCollecting aiosqlite==0.22.1 (from theHarvester==5.0.0)\n  Using cached aiosqlite-0.22.1-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (4.3 kB)\nCollecting beautifulsoup4==4.15.0 (from theHarvester==5.0.0)\n  Using cached beautifulsoup4-4.15.0-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (3.8 kB)\nCollecting certifi==2026.6.17 